  "faq_heading": "Surrey schools: your questions answered",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The BC Ministry of Education and Child Care school list shows 168 schools with a Surrey street address: 137 public schools and 31 independent schools. It also shows 9 college and university campuses. In that list, 15 schools marked as offering French Immersion, 1 Francophone school run by the Conseil scolaire francophone, 3 alternate programs and 4 online schools."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public schools here are run by School District 36 (Surrey) and School District 93 (Conseil scolaire francophone). Count by district: School District 36 (Surrey): 136, School District 93 (Conseil scolaire francophone): 1."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Alternate programs, continuing education centres and online schools that have a street address sit under \"other public schools and programs\"; the level of every school is read from its name."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public secondary schools with a Surrey address: Clayton Heights Secondary, Earl Marriott Secondary, Elgin Park Secondary, Enver Creek Secondary, Fleetwood Park Secondary, Frank Hurt Secondary, Fraser Heights Secondary and Grandview Heights Secondary and 14 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Ministry file marks these Surrey schools as offering French Immersion: Crescent Park Elementary, Earl Marriott Secondary, Jessie Lee Elementary, K B Woodward Elementary, Kwantlen Park Secondary, Laronde Elementary, Martha Currie Elementary, Pacific Heights Elementary, Sikh Academy and Simon Cunningham Elementary and 5 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Independent schools listed for Surrey include Al-Mustafa School, Anchor Point Montessori, Bibleway Christian Academy, Cloverdale Catholic School, Cornerstone Montessori School and Crescent Heights Academy and 25 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Before an offer, ask the district which school serves the exact street address."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Surrey school district publishes its catchments only as an interactive map, not as a list of streets. Use the district's own page to check an address:",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Surrey school district catchments and school finder",
      "h": "https://www.surreyschools.ca/school-locator",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Conseil scolaire francophone publishes its attendance zones (zones de fréquentation) on its own site:",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Conseil scolaire francophone attendance zones",
      "h": "https://www.csf.bc.ca/transport/zones-de-frequentation/",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The district's own school pages also list French Immersion at Crescent Park Elementary, Earl Marriott Secondary, Jessie Lee Elementary, K B Woodward Elementary, Kwantlen Park Secondary, Laronde Elementary, Martha Currie Elementary, Pacific Heights Elementary, Simon Cunningham Elementary, Snokomish Elementary, Sunrise Ridge Elementary, and École Panorama Ridge Secondary and 2 more, where the Ministry file flag reads No. Confirm the program with the school before relying on either.",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The list covers the whole city, so schools in South Surrey, Cloverdale, Newton, Fleetwood and Guildford are in it because they carry Surrey addresses."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Read how South Surrey school catchments work",
      "h": "/south-surrey-school-catchments.html"
    },
